    "operator": "Change the digit replacement for 9 from the two-digit string 10 to the two-digit string 11. Each digit 0..8 is still replaced by d+1; replacements in one operation remain simultaneous.",
    "correctness_argument": "Each digit evolves independently. DP f[m][d] is f[m-1][d+1] for d<9 and f[m-1][1]+f[m-1][0] for d=9; the L3 latter term is f[m-1][1] twice. Sum over initial digits. The independent oracle enumerates the descendant tree and counts leaves, skipping only nonbranching increments until each digit9 split. Explicit stacks keep memory bounded and prevent recursive stack overflow in L2.",
